# Day 56

**30km / 7 hours**

*Whanganui to Koitiata*

Back on my feet again, this time on the road out of Whanganui. The path alongside the river is pretty nice although the rain had returned after being thankfully absent all canoe journey. Then after going on a more rural road and passing the small airport and a defence area with army peeps larping with guns which was a little disconcerting.

![We meet the beach again](./beach.avif)

Then it was back to the beach once more. This was a bit more miserable than the last beach stretches because of the rain that was coming and going. After trudging on the beach for a while there was a river and the track went up the river to get to the fancy new bridge across it. It was a nice bridge although there were some narrow steel bollards across the front of it that were difficult to the get the pack past.

![The cool bridge](./bridge.avif)

![The view from the bridge](./bridge-view.avif)

More beach again! Another few hours of that before the final river just before the town with a campground. However I had got there just about high tide and there was no bridge for this one so it was either wait or try to get through anyway. There were three other guys who basically took off their clothes, put their packs on their heads and trudged through which worked but looked miserably cold with some risk so I cowardly waited for a bit and ate some food. Eventually I got bored of that as the rain returned so went near the mouth of the river where it met the sea and made the cold walk through. 

It got to about waist high or slightly above but only at the end and I was able to get through without disaster although I was soaking wet and quite cold when I got in to the campground of the town. In the evening the rain cleared to give a nice sunset which was a positive to not a great day.

![The sun setting on a poor day](./sunset.avif)